# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# Store every text file as LF in the repository and check it out as LF on
# every platform, regardless of the machine's core.autocrlf setting. Without
# this, autocrlf=true checkouts (and `pnpm format`) flip CRLF<->LF on tracked
# files and light up `git status` with ~80 phantom "modified" entries, forcing
# fragile stage-by-name discipline and risking accidental mass-normalisation
# commits. See workspace memory `fuaran-live-crlf-working-tree-trap`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalise (defensive; none tracked today, but sample
# apps may grow images/fonts later).
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.pdf   binary
